   "suggestions": [
    {
     "field": "scenario_contexts",
     "severity": "Medium",
     "issue": "The scenario \"Explaining to a student why -6 dB is not 'half' the height on a linear waveform view\" is a learning trap: on a LINEAR amplitude (waveform) display, -6 dB IS approximately half the height (10^(-6/20) = 0.5). As written the statement is backwards and would teach the student a falsehood, undercutting the entry's own linear-vs-log lesson.",
     "suggestion": "Reword to put the misconception on the dB scale, e.g.: \"Explaining to a student that -6 dB sits near the TOP of a dB meter, not halfway down, even though it is about half the amplitude on a linear waveform view.\" This preserves the intended teaching point without stating something false."
    }
